preConditionHook:
// EL: topTail = high - maxlist(open, close); botTail = minlist(open, close) -
// low. Both measured from the body edge, so the test does not care which way
// the bar closed. MinList/MaxList are ACCEPTED for tick-grid PRICE operands
// only (EL_FEATURES.md), and the open and the close are raw prices -- they
// differ by exactly 0 or by at least one tick, 1e9-1e11x the 2.22e-12
// relational tolerance -- so the plain ternary stand-in is exact, the same
// arrangement BarOverlapFraction uses. (<algorithm> is not among the emitted
// includes, so no std::min/std::max.)
//
// No body term and no direction, which is the whole difference from
// StrongTrendBar: a shaved doji passes this and fails that. Multiplied, never
// a ratio, so a zero-range bar reads 0 <= 0 on both tails and passes instead
// of raising EL's runtime divide-by-zero.
topTail = high[0] - (open[0] > close[0] ? open[0] : close[0]);
botTail = (open[0] < close[0] ? open[0] : close[0]) - low[0];
barRange = high[0] - low[0];
